@prefix tmodel: <https://threat-radar.github.io/tmodel/schema/object-model/> .
@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix sh: <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#> .
tmodel:Assertion a sh:NodeShape ;
	rdfs:comment "Reified edge (§4): subject / predicate / object, so a Review, confidence, and provenance can point at the statement. Substrate-neutral logical node; RDF-star, named graphs, and LPG edge-properties are storage lowerings (ADR-0004) and are not chosen here. Promoting a reviewed edge to this node narrows DEC-004 (no pure edge-property-only form for reviewed assertions). The acceptance gate (provenance + review before status=accepted) is a hand-written constraint, not something gen-shacl emits (§13)." ;
	sh:closed true ;
	sh:ignoredProperties _:c14n128 ;
	sh:property _:c14n109 , _:c14n190 , _:c14n254 , _:c14n275 , _:c14n28 , _:c14n338 , _:c14n358 , _:c14n402 , _:c14n427 , _:c14n488 , _:c14n80 , _:c14n89 ;
	sh:targetClass tmodel:Assertion .
tmodel:Asset a sh:NodeShape ;
	rdfs:comment "Accepted via ADR-0011 (DL-0024). Something worth protecting: the thing damage happens to (ARCH-0001 §3). In ISO/SAE 21434 terms (3.1.2, as paraphrased in RPT-0007), it has value and one or more cybersecurity properties whose compromise can lead to a damage scenario. Maps OTM `assets` and threagile data assets. Data, functions and the vehicle itself can all be assets; where an asset lives is `stored_in` / `processed_by`." ;
	sh:closed true ;
	sh:ignoredProperties _:c14n492 ;
	sh:property _:c14n143 , _:c14n158 , _:c14n246 , _:c14n266 , _:c14n321 , _:c14n346 , _:c14n383 ;
	sh:targetClass tmodel:Asset .
tmodel:AttackPath a sh:NodeShape ;
	rdfs:comment "An ordered set of AttackSteps realising a ThreatInstance (§2a, §3). Feasibility is rated here, at path level (human-rated at MVP). Feasibility METHOD is ISO/SAE 21434 Table-1 (§3, DL-0011), human-rated at MVP; Common Criteria is display-only (numbers + label). No per-step aggregation at MVP. DEC-003 is open; ADR-0005 was dropped, not accepted." ;
	sh:closed true ;
	sh:ignoredProperties _:c14n284 ;
	sh:property _:c14n215 , _:c14n296 , _:c14n355 , _:c14n362 , _:c14n365 , _:c14n479 , _:c14n79 ;
	sh:targetClass tmodel:AttackPath .
tmodel:AttackPattern a sh:NodeShape ;
	rdfs:comment "Generic attack pattern (CAPEC / ATT&CK technique = *what*, §1, §2a). STRIDE is not a property of this class (§2). Kill-chain phase is on AttackStep, not here." ;
	sh:closed true ;
	sh:ignoredProperties _:c14n50 ;
	sh:property _:c14n104 , _:c14n183 , _:c14n410 , _:c14n48 ;
	sh:targetClass tmodel:AttackPattern .
tmodel:AttackStep a sh:NodeShape ;
	rdfs:comment "A step in an attack graph (§2a): AND/OR `gate`, explicit `precedes` order, shareable across paths. Optional kill-chain phase is coarse order, not the ATT&CK technique. Pre/postconditions are not given a schema shape in §2a." ;
	sh:closed true ;
	sh:ignoredProperties _:c14n417 ;
	sh:property _:c14n235 , _:c14n263 , _:c14n268 , _:c14n31 , _:c14n320 , _:c14n332 ;
	sh:targetClass tmodel:AttackStep .
tmodel:Checkpoint a sh:NodeShape ;
	rdfs:comment "A lighter, recurring review point on a SecurityProgram (§3c R-041) — a ProgramNode with no extra shape; it reuses `gated_by` / `decided_by` / `at_phase`. Corporate SDLs name these variously (checkpoint, review, stage)." ;
	sh:closed true ;
	sh:ignoredProperties _:c14n501 ;
	sh:property _:c14n126 , _:c14n135 , _:c14n142 , _:c14n191 , _:c14n2 , _:c14n240 , _:c14n243 , _:c14n415 , _:c14n448 , _:c14n459 , _:c14n94 , _:c14n96 ;
	sh:targetClass tmodel:Checkpoint .
tmodel:Component a sh:NodeShape ;
	rdfs:comment "Authoritative deployed artifact (service, container, dependency, chip, core). Since ADR-0011 it is also the end of a DataFlow and a member of a trust zone, as an OTM component is; the field-level OTM crosswalk stays with #9 (§0). `uses_component` / `composed_of` are the propagation paths for vulnerabilities (§5)." ;
	sh:closed true ;
	sh:ignoredProperties _:c14n93 ;
	sh:property _:c14n10 , _:c14n179 , _:c14n193 , _:c14n264 , _:c14n325 , _:c14n416 , _:c14n420 , _:c14n429 , _:c14n456 , _:c14n462 , _:c14n54 , _:c14n69 , _:c14n9 ;
	sh:targetClass tmodel:Component .
tmodel:DamageScenario a sh:NodeShape ;
	rdfs:comment "The damage a ThreatInstance realizes (§1). Impact categories are recorded on RiskScore, not collapsed here (§3)." ;
	sh:closed true ;
	sh:ignoredProperties _:c14n159 ;
	sh:property _:c14n124 , _:c14n155 , _:c14n185 , _:c14n242 , _:c14n295 ;
	sh:targetClass tmodel:DamageScenario .
tmodel:DataFlow a sh:NodeShape ;
	rdfs:comment "Accepted via ADR-0011 (DL-0024). A directed flow of data or commands from one Component to another (OTM `dataflows`, threagile communication links, CycloneDX service `data` flows), carrying Assets. ADR-0011 joins Components directly, which is OTM's shape and needs no DFD classes. The proposal's §1 puts DataFlow in a behavioral DFD layer, between Process, DataStore and ExternalEntity elements `realized_by` Components; a later ADR that adds that layer would widen `flow_from` and `flow_to`. Threats on a flow (spoofing, tampering, disclosure) point at it through ThreatInstance.targets_element." ;
	sh:closed true ;
	sh:ignoredProperties _:c14n334 ;
	sh:property _:c14n0 , _:c14n207 , _:c14n283 , _:c14n386 , _:c14n397 , _:c14n436 , _:c14n487 , _:c14n6 , _:c14n60 ;
	sh:targetClass tmodel:DataFlow .
tmodel:Deployment a sh:NodeShape ;
	rdfs:comment "A placement of one ProductInstance (§3). Many Deployments per instance; each points at one Environment. Single deployment is the MVP assumption; deployment-relative risk (R-023) is post-MVP." ;
	sh:closed true ;
	sh:ignoredProperties _:c14n310 ;
	sh:property _:c14n148 , _:c14n230 , _:c14n311 , _:c14n428 , _:c14n438 ;
	sh:targetClass tmodel:Deployment .
tmodel:Environment a sh:NodeShape ;
	rdfs:comment "Reusable operational exposure of a running deployment (§3, F9): physical security, connectivity, operational context. Parameterises feasibility's exploitability side only — never impact CIA (F5). Distinct from LifecyclePhase (§3b). The MVP metric runs without requiring this node." ;
	sh:closed true ;
	sh:ignoredProperties _:c14n490 ;
	sh:property _:c14n107 , _:c14n180 , _:c14n32 , _:c14n337 , _:c14n453 , _:c14n95 ;
	sh:targetClass tmodel:Environment .
tmodel:Gate a sh:NodeShape ;
	rdfs:comment "A named, ordered, dated DECISION point with exit criteria and an approving Review (§3c R-041). Its exit criterion runs the conformance check (`validates_conformance_of` a ThreatModel): a model is conformant when every in-scope ThreatInstance has an approved, evidenced Mitigation (R-042). The check PROVES linkage + approval, NOT adequacy — the human cybersecurity-assessment judgement stays a human input (CLAUDE.md)." ;
	sh:closed true ;
	sh:ignoredProperties _:c14n432 ;
	sh:property _:c14n105 , _:c14n130 , _:c14n157 , _:c14n17 , _:c14n19 , _:c14n195 , _:c14n196 , _:c14n222 , _:c14n234 , _:c14n286 , _:c14n42 , _:c14n463 , _:c14n470 ;
	sh:targetClass tmodel:Gate .
tmodel:GovernedView a sh:NodeShape ;
	rdfs:comment "The governed, persisted subtype of View (§3c R-043). The existing `View` stays the TRANSIENT lens (query/projection, never written back); a GovernedView is the TRACKED artifact — an owned / approved / reproducible snapshot. It keeps View's `projection`/`focus_query` and adds governance: `owner` (Party ROLE, §2b), `revision` (the saved view's version), approval via the Review spine (`approved_by`) pinned to an `approval_digest` so the sign-off is reproducible against KG state at a point in time (SysML v2 View/Viewpoint, OMG SACM, OSCAL→Word prior art), `governance_status`, and `supersedes`. `renders` the KG scope it materializes (e.g. a ThreatModel or SecurityProgram). Post-MVP." ;
	sh:closed true ;
	sh:ignoredProperties _:c14n197 ;
	sh:property _:c14n103 , _:c14n111 , _:c14n170 , _:c14n22 , _:c14n301 , _:c14n349 , _:c14n364 , _:c14n375 , _:c14n379 , _:c14n384 , _:c14n395 , _:c14n499 , _:c14n66 , _:c14n78 , _:c14n85 ;
	sh:targetClass tmodel:GovernedView .
tmodel:ImpactVector a sh:NodeShape ;
	rdfs:comment "Inlined value object for RiskScore.impact (§3). ISO 21434 safety / financial / operational / privacy, each severe|major|moderate|negligible. Keeping the four categories is the method; collapsing to one number is display-only. Not a §13 domain class. business_impact is a different post-MVP axis and is not a field here." ;
	sh:closed true ;
	sh:ignoredProperties _:c14n228 ;
	sh:property _:c14n141 , _:c14n306 , _:c14n374 , _:c14n482 ;
	sh:targetClass tmodel:ImpactVector .
tmodel:LifecyclePhase a sh:NodeShape ;
	rdfs:comment "Coarse lifecycle stage (§3b). The vocabulary is LifecyclePhaseCode (concept through decommission/disposal, ISO 21434 + ISO 26262 aligned). Reverse-logistics transitions and custody provenance are post-MVP and are not modeled. `name` is the human label; `code` is the enum." ;
	sh:closed true ;
	sh:ignoredProperties _:c14n314 ;
	sh:property _:c14n335 , _:c14n336 , _:c14n354 , _:c14n90 ;
	sh:targetClass tmodel:LifecyclePhase .
tmodel:Milestone a sh:NodeShape ;
	rdfs:comment "A dated, owned deliverable point on a SecurityProgram (§3c R-041), optionally dated relative to another node (`offset_from`). May serve as a gate entry condition via another node's `depends_on_node`." ;
	sh:closed true ;
	sh:ignoredProperties _:c14n134 ;
	sh:property _:c14n100 , _:c14n110 , _:c14n144 , _:c14n172 , _:c14n205 , _:c14n217 , _:c14n257 , _:c14n3 , _:c14n316 , _:c14n343 , _:c14n44 , _:c14n476 , _:c14n51 ;
	sh:targetClass tmodel:Milestone .
tmodel:Mitigation a sh:NodeShape ;
	rdfs:comment "A mitigation/control (catalog example D3FEND, §1). §5 instance fields (implementation owner, external work-item refs, status) are on this class until a separate MitigationInstance class is accepted. Status is also surfaced as RiskScore.mitigation_status (R-045) — a peer of the derived risk, not an input to it. A GENERIC mitigation for a product type/family is `stated_as` a Requirement (technical, process, audit, …); a product-specific mitigation discharges that Requirement through `Requirement.satisfied_by` (ADR-0012)." ;
	sh:closed true ;
	sh:ignoredProperties _:c14n77 ;
	sh:property _:c14n146 , _:c14n174 , _:c14n208 , _:c14n25 , _:c14n255 , _:c14n356 , _:c14n458 , _:c14n65 , _:c14n86 , _:c14n99 ;
	sh:targetClass tmodel:Mitigation .
tmodel:Node a sh:NodeShape ;
	rdfs:comment "Shared identity for every §13 class. `id` is the stable object id ADR-0004 requires across file, LPG, and RDF encodings. Not itself a §13 class." ;
	sh:closed false ;
	sh:ignoredProperties _:c14n323 ;
	sh:property _:c14n160 , _:c14n382 , _:c14n424 ;
	sh:targetClass tmodel:Node .
tmodel:Party a sh:NodeShape ;
	rdfs:comment "One reusable identity for an organization or a person (§2b). ThreatActor and PROV Agent are facets of this identity, not separate §13 classes. Only intrinsic classifications live on the node; supplier/owner/vendor-of are edges." ;
	sh:closed true ;
	sh:ignoredProperties _:c14n381 ;
	sh:property _:c14n345 , _:c14n357 , _:c14n435 , _:c14n452 , _:c14n494 ;
	sh:targetClass tmodel:Party .
tmodel:Product a sh:NodeShape ;
	rdfs:comment "A product design (structural layer, §1). Recursive composition is `composed_of` Components (§3). Relational party roles are edges (§2b). `classifications` names the product types / families it belongs to (e.g. `family:connected-ecu`); a Requirement scoped to a family by `applies_to_family` applies to every Product carrying that value (ADR-0012). There is no ProductFamily class (DEC-009)." ;
	sh:closed true ;
	sh:ignoredProperties _:c14n359 ;
	sh:property _:c14n154 , _:c14n20 , _:c14n226 , _:c14n298 , _:c14n317 , _:c14n327 , _:c14n367 , _:c14n391 , _:c14n98 ;
	sh:targetClass tmodel:Product .
tmodel:ProductInstance a sh:NodeShape ;
	rdfs:comment "A versioned, identity-bearing instance of a Product (§1, §3b). Lifecycle *state* sits here (with valid_from/valid_to), not on Product or Component. A refurbished unit can share a firmware hash and still carry a new phase, Deployment, and owner. The firmware image digest / build hash is an opaque `identifiers` string (ADR-0002 per-type instance identity), not a pinned slot." ;
	sh:closed true ;
	sh:ignoredProperties _:c14n209 ;
	sh:property _:c14n151 , _:c14n18 , _:c14n204 , _:c14n218 , _:c14n331 , _:c14n369 , _:c14n399 , _:c14n405 , _:c14n421 , _:c14n433 , _:c14n52 ;
	sh:targetClass tmodel:ProductInstance .
tmodel:ProgramNode a sh:NodeShape ;
	rdfs:comment "Shared shape for an SDL program node (§3c R-041): a named, `order`-ed, dated governance point on a SecurityProgram, mapped onto the LifecyclePhase axis (§3b, `at_phase`). Carries program-management fields — `order`, `planned_date` vs `actual_date`, `gate_status`, `owner` (Party ROLE, §2b), the Requirements that gate passage (`gated_by`), the Reviews that decide it (`decided_by` — the §4 human-review spine, not a parallel mechanism), and node dependencies / entry criteria (`depends_on_node`). Corporate gate-naming varies, so `name` is the local label and `at_phase` the canonical mapping (MAP-0001 gate crosswalk). Not instantiated directly; use Gate / Milestone / Checkpoint." ;
	sh:closed false ;
	sh:ignoredProperties _:c14n236 ;
	sh:property _:c14n125 , _:c14n260 , _:c14n278 , _:c14n285 , _:c14n303 , _:c14n350 , _:c14n404 , _:c14n41 , _:c14n419 , _:c14n484 , _:c14n5 , _:c14n76 ;
	sh:targetClass tmodel:ProgramNode .
tmodel:RedundancyGroup a sh:NodeShape ;
	rdfs:comment "Marks Deployments (or whole build/review systems) as replicas (§3, §10): `replica_of` / `redundant_with`. Supports common-mode risk and per-replica mitigation divergence. Post-MVP (R-034)." ;
	sh:closed true ;
	sh:ignoredProperties _:c14n63 ;
	sh:property _:c14n224 , _:c14n231 , _:c14n411 , _:c14n460 , _:c14n498 ;
	sh:targetClass tmodel:RedundancyGroup .
tmodel:Requirement a sh:NodeShape ;
	rdfs:comment "CORE (ADR-0012, amending ADR-0010 / DEC-001a). A normative statement a product must meet: taken from a standard, regulation or guideline (ISO/SAE 21434, ETSI EN 304 223, NIST SP 800-218, …) or authored for a product type/family. `text` is the statement and `text_origin` says whether it is a paraphrase, verbatim or authored; for a licensed standard it is ALWAYS a paraphrase and the clause is in `source_locator`. `source_ref` is an OPAQUE uriorcurie into the library requirement record (Threat-Radar/library) — tmodel aligns by reference ONLY; it does not import or depend on the library schema. `requirement_kind` classifies it (technical / process / audit / documentation / organizational / other) and `normativity` says how binding it is. Edges: `refines` / `derived_from` / `conflicts_with` / `maps_to` (overlap, the MAP-0001 crosswalk) to other Requirements; `addresses` the ThreatInstance / Weakness / AttackPattern it counters; `satisfied_by` the Mitigation(s) that discharge it; `applies_to` a Product / ProductInstance / Component, or `applies_to_family` a product type/family (matched against Product.classifications). A generic Mitigation is `stated_as` a Requirement. AI-proposed requirement links are `proposed` Assertions until a human Review accepts them (§4). `conformance_status` is NOT accepted: it is the DEC-001b R-042 verdict (C1) and stays proposal-level; core vectors do not set it." ;
	sh:closed true ;
	sh:ignoredProperties _:c14n199 ;
	sh:property _:c14n114 , _:c14n140 , _:c14n188 , _:c14n21 , _:c14n244 , _:c14n259 , _:c14n261 , _:c14n265 , _:c14n270 , _:c14n307 , _:c14n318 , _:c14n347 , _:c14n439 , _:c14n440 , _:c14n473 , _:c14n478 , _:c14n70 , _:c14n8 ;
	sh:targetClass tmodel:Requirement .
tmodel:Review a sh:NodeShape ;
	rdfs:comment "Human verdict on an Assertion (§4, §5). Kept separate from the proposal. Carries status, priority, and justification. STIX Opinion/Note is a future mapping (DEC-002 / #9), not a parent class." ;
	sh:closed true ;
	sh:ignoredProperties _:c14n73 ;
	sh:property _:c14n113 , _:c14n171 , _:c14n194 , _:c14n212 , _:c14n225 , _:c14n262 , _:c14n425 , _:c14n457 ;
	sh:targetClass tmodel:Review .
tmodel:RiskScore a sh:NodeShape ;
	rdfs:comment "Composite risk vector (sponsor round, proposed.10 / DL-0011; DEC-003 OPEN — ADR-0005 was dropped, not accepted). Peer slots: feasibility (ISO 21434 Table-1 method; Common Criteria display-only — numbers, label, and a colored indicator in table views), impact (from attack damage; 21434 S/F/O/P), mitigation_status, and derived risk. Shown alongside its inputs, never instead of them. Not a single CVSS score. More components only with a further sponsor decision. MVP: one stakeholder; business_impact is post-MVP and intentionally has no slot." ;
	sh:closed true ;
	sh:ignoredProperties _:c14n11 ;
	sh:property _:c14n162 , _:c14n168 , _:c14n233 , _:c14n274 , _:c14n282 , _:c14n313 , _:c14n36 , _:c14n378 , _:c14n408 , _:c14n43 , _:c14n437 ;
	sh:targetClass tmodel:RiskScore .
tmodel:SecurityProgram a sh:NodeShape ;
	rdfs:comment "The SDL as a first-class, GOVERNED, VERSIONED object (§3c R-041). An ordered, named, dated program `governs` a Product / ProductInstance / ProductFamily and is composed of `program_nodes` (Gate / Milestone / Checkpoint) mapped onto the LifecyclePhase axis (§3b, each node's `at_phase`). It `incorporates` the Requirements it enforces; its gates run the conformance check (R-042). Full program management lives on the program nodes (owner, planned/actual dates, status per node). It is itself a governed view (owner / revision / approved_by + approval_digest / governance_status / supersedes), reconciling §10 \"views are transient\": the SDL plan is a named, versioned, signed-off snapshot over the one SoT, iterating across review cycles. Post-MVP." ;
	sh:closed true ;
	sh:ignoredProperties _:c14n276 ;
	sh:property _:c14n129 , _:c14n138 , _:c14n176 , _:c14n288 , _:c14n292 , _:c14n308 , _:c14n352 , _:c14n360 , _:c14n389 , _:c14n398 , _:c14n483 , _:c14n500 , _:c14n61 , _:c14n68 , _:c14n87 ;
	sh:targetClass tmodel:SecurityProgram .
tmodel:ThreatInstance a sh:NodeShape ;
	rdfs:comment "A threat in a model, not the generic catalog entry (§1). Carries the method facet (STRIDE and, post-MVP, LINDDUN/MAESTRO) and `realizes` a DamageScenario. Phase scope is `applies_in_phase` (§3b), distinct from Environment." ;
	sh:closed true ;
	sh:ignoredProperties _:c14n486 ;
	sh:property _:c14n13 , _:c14n181 , _:c14n305 , _:c14n348 , _:c14n401 , _:c14n422 , _:c14n45 , _:c14n471 , _:c14n72 ;
	sh:targetClass tmodel:ThreatInstance .
tmodel:ThreatModel a sh:NodeShape ;
	rdfs:comment "A GOVERNED, VERSIONED view/snapshot over the KG-as-SoT (§3c R-043). NOT domain truth re-stated: a reviewed LENS whose membership and verdicts are tracked across review cycles. Scope is either a bounded `scope_query` or an explicit `members` set (in-scope ThreatInstances / AttackPaths / Components / Products). Governance is the shared governed-view facet: `owner` (a Party ROLE, §2b — not a new actor type), `revision`, approval through the existing Review spine (`approved_by`) pinned to an `approval_digest` so sign-off is REPRODUCIBLE against KG state at a point in time, `governance_status` (draft/in-review/approved/superseded), and `supersedes` the prior revision. ARCH-0001 has no ThreatModel class; this is the scope node for \"the threat model itself\" (RPT-0013-OM §2). Post-MVP as an SDL object (the threat content it scopes is MVP)." ;
	sh:closed true ;
	sh:ignoredProperties _:c14n475 ;
	sh:property _:c14n156 , _:c14n16 , _:c14n169 , _:c14n186 , _:c14n187 , _:c14n192 , _:c14n315 , _:c14n342 , _:c14n370 , _:c14n454 , _:c14n489 , _:c14n497 , _:c14n59 , _:c14n62 ;
	sh:targetClass tmodel:ThreatModel .
tmodel:TrustBoundary a sh:NodeShape ;
	rdfs:comment "Accepted via ADR-0011 (DL-0024). Where control or assumptions change (ARCH-0001 §3), modeled as a zone, as the proposal's §1 does: a Component is `in_trust_zone` a TrustBoundary (§1, F12), and zones nest through `within_boundary`, which can also name the Component a zone sits inside, because an OTM trust zone's `parent` may be a component. A DataFlow whose ends sit in different zones crosses the boundary between them; `crosses_boundary` states it explicitly where membership is unknown. Maps OTM `trustZones` and pytm boundaries; threagile's member lists and CycloneDX's per-service `trustZone` import onto the same zone (RPT-0005 crosswalk, \"four shapes\"). `zone_type` and `trust_level` keep the source's own labels." ;
	sh:closed true ;
	sh:ignoredProperties _:c14n491 ;
	sh:property _:c14n122 , _:c14n132 , _:c14n239 , _:c14n371 , _:c14n38 , _:c14n468 ;
	sh:targetClass tmodel:TrustBoundary .
tmodel:View a sh:NodeShape ;
	rdfs:comment "Derived presentation lens (§10): query/filter + projection. Not domain truth and never written back onto domain nodes. Saved views may be persisted; rendered geometry is transient and out of this schema. One graph projection is MVP; other projections are post-MVP." ;
	sh:closed true ;
	sh:ignoredProperties _:c14n182 ;
